ons are straightforward. There's no ambiguity in the information provided, so the answer should be A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe statement is true because Barutin Cove, named after a Bulgarian settlement, is located in Antarctica via the South Shetland Islands.\n\n**Answer: A) True**",
