      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement \"Basque is a Romance language\" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break down the information step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that all Romance languages are Indo-European languages. That means if a language is Romance, it must be Indo-European. Also, Romance languages form a language family, and within a language family, all languages are related to each other. So, French and Spanish are both Romance languages, which makes sense because they're both in the same family and related.\n\nThen, it mentions that German is related to Spanish. Wait, but German isn't a Romance language. I know German is a Germanic language, which is a different branch of the Indo-European family. So, if German is related to Spanish, that might mean they share some common roots but aren't in the same language family. Maybe they both come from the same proto-language but diverged into different branches.\n\nNext, Basque is described as not related to any other language. That's interesting because it's a language isolate, meaning it doesn't have any known relatives. So, Basque isn't part of the Indo-European family, including the Romance languages.\n\nNow, the question is whether Basque is a Romance language. From the context, Romance languages are a subset of Indo-European languages. Since Basque isn't related to any other language, it can't be part of the Indo-European family, and therefore, it can't be a Romance language. So the statement should be false.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I'm not missing anything. The context says all Romance languages are Indo-European, but it doesn't say that all Indo-European languages are Romance. So, Romance is just one branch. Basque isn't Indo-European, so it's definitely not Romance. Yeah, that makes sense.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Basque is a Romance language\" is false because Basque is not related to any other language and is not part of the Indo-European family, which includes Romance languages.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
