fect the conditional.\n\nBut the problem is that we don't know if Greyhound has planes or not. The context doesn't mention anything about Greyhound having planes. So, the conditional only tells us about the absence of planes if they aren't an airline, but it doesn't confirm their status as an airline.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, we can't determine for certain whether Greyhound is an airline. It's uncertain because the context doesn't provide enough information to confirm or deny it.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Greyhound is an airline\" is uncertain based on the given information. The context provides a conditional statement about Greyhound not being an airline leading to no Greyhound planes, but it doesn't confirm Greyhound's status as an airline. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Uncertain",
